{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":97311,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6830b977-a6f9-55bc-b7e2-07f45327c0e1","total_cost_usd":0.756397,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12280,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10070,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12280,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10070,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12280},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7202,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0072770000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10070,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12280,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.74912,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:v200b-reviewer-fable-01\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:533703c9e99aabc44ace\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"In case:533703c9e99aabc44ace, the selected result labels 37.5 percent as the 'Fledging rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest sites' while the rate is computed as 18 events divided by only the 48 retained post-screening sites; the 12 screened-out planned sites are excluded from the denominator, so a retained-subset statistic is attributed to the complete planned domain that the task designates as the scientific target.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow sets the rate denominator to the retained subset count (analysis.py: 'denominator = retained_units', yielding 48) after screening out 12 of the 60 planned sites, but the report template attaches that subset-based rate to a claim scoped to the complete planned set of 60 sites, with no protocol amendment or approved deviation to redefine the target.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The governing task requires the reported rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = complete planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result claims the rate for the complete planned set of 60 sites while computing it with a denominator of 48 retained sites (18/48 = 37.5%).\", \"observed_value\": {\"claimed_domain_n\": 60, \"denominator_used\": 48, \"events\": 18, \"rate_pct\": 37.5}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Fledging rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest sites: 37.5 percent (proportion 0.3750), computed as 18 confirmed fledging events divided by 48 nest sites.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow explicitly assigns the retained-subset count as the rate denominator.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator = retained_units (48 of 60 planned)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 50, \"end_line\": 51, \"quoted_text\": \"denominator = retained_units\\n    rate = Fraction(events, denominator)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's own accounting shows 60 planned units, 48 retained, and 12 removed by screening, confirming the denominator equals the retained subset rather than the planned set.\", \"observed_value\": {\"planned\": 60, \"retained\": 48, \"removed\": 12}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 10, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned nest sites: 60\\n- Retained after screening: 48\\n- Removed by screening: 12\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report states no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists, so no authorization redefines the target from the complete planned set to the retained subset.\", \"observed_value\": \"no amendment or deviation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 27, \"end_line\": 27, \"quoted_text\": \"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exist for this analysis.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The selected result transparently discloses the actual denominator ('divided by 48 nest sites'), so a careful reader can detect the mismatch; one could argue the disclosure mitigates the misattribution. However, the headline claim still binds 37.5 percent to 'the complete planned set of 60 nest sites', which is the misattribution the issue class describes, and disclosure of the computation does not change the claimed domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator disclosed in-line as 48\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"computed as 18 confirmed fledging events divided by 48 nest sites\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The screening is described as prespecified and the removed sites have unknown outcomes, so 18/48 could be defended as a complete-case estimate; but the task and the report's own scientific-target section fix the target as the complete planned set of 60, and the claim presents the subset rate as the rate 'for' that complete set rather than as a retained-subset estimate.\", \"observed_value\": \"screening prespecified; removed outcomes unknown\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Prespecified screening step: a nest site is eligible only if camera uptime over the\\nincubation window is at least 80.0 percent. 12 planned sites fell below that threshold\\nand were removed; their fledging outcome is recorded as unknown.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 6, \"quoted_text\": \"The scientific target is the complete planned set of 60 monitored guillemot nest sites\\nin the 2025 Cape Rendel breeding-season monitoring plan.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to defeat the verdict three ways. (1) Checked whether the claim is actually scoped to the retained subset: the selected result says 'for the complete planned set of 60 nest sites', so no. (2) Checked whether any amendment or deviation legitimizes a subset denominator for a complete-domain claim: the report states none exists. (3) Recomputed from inputs/data.csv: exactly 12 sites have camera_uptime_pct < 80.0 (4 per sector), leaving 48 retained; 18/48 = 37.5% matches the report, while the complete-domain accounting would use 60 as denominator (18/60 = 30.0%). The mismatch between claimed domain (60) and denominator used (48) survives all three checks.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:575a0b1399c85e4cf4d7\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The governing task explicitly defines the scientific target as the retained post-screening subset, not the complete planned set.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = retained post-screening subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result is scoped to the retained subset ('of the retained subset', 'Among the 15 retained vernal pools') and uses the retained subset count 15 as denominator, matching the declared target.\", \"observed_value\": {\"claimed_domain_n\": 15, \"denominator_used\": 15, \"events\": 9, \"rate_pct\": 60.0}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among the 15 retained vernal pools, wood frog egg masses were detected in 9 pools, a detection rate of 60.00% (9/15) of the retained subset.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly distinguishes the retained-subset target from the complete planned set and states the screened-out pools are excluded by design, so no claim is attributed to the complete domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"retained subset explicitly distinguished from planned set of 20\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"The scientific target is defined explicitly and only as the 15\\nretained pools that met the prespecified hydroperiod eligibility\\ncriterion (>= 60 days of standing water). Every claim below is\\nconfined to that retained subset and is distinct from the complete\\nplanned set of 20 pools; the 5 screened-out pools are excluded\\nfrom the denominator by design.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Independent recomputation from inputs/data.csv confirms 15 pools with hydroperiod_days >= 60 (P04, P07, P10, P13, P17 removed) and 9 of those 15 with egg_mass_detected = yes, matching the reported 9/15 = 60.00%.\", \"observed_value\": {\"retained_recount\": 15, \"removed_recount\": 5, \"events_recount\": 9}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 21, \"quoted_text\": \"pool_id,hydroperiod_days,egg_mass_detected\\nP01,74,yes\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 11, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"retained = [\\n        r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"hydroperiod_days\\\"]) >= MIN_HYDROPERIOD_DAYS\\n    ]\\n    retained_n = len(retained)\\n    removed_n = planned - retained_n\\n    events = sum(1 for r in retained if r[\\\"egg_mass_detected\\\"] == \\\"yes\\\")\\n    rate = f\\\"{100.0 * events / retained_n:.2f}\\\"\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The rate does exclude 5 of the 20 planned pools from the denominator, which is the mechanical precondition for the issue class; this would demonstrate the issue only if the claim were attributed to the complete planned domain. It is not: both the task and every claim in the report scope the result to the retained subset, so the exclusion matches the declared target.\", \"observed_value\": \"5 planned pools excluded, consistent with declared subset target\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned survey pools: 20\\n- Retained after hydroperiod screening (>= 60 days): 15\\n- Removed by screening (< 60 days): 5\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I searched for any statement attributing the 60.00% rate, or any other rate, to the complete planned set of 20 pools; none exists — the title, target section, and selected result all confine claims to the 15 retained pools, and the report affirmatively distinguishes the subset from the planned set. I also recomputed retention and events from the raw data (15 retained, 9 detections) to rule out a hidden denominator mismatch, and confirmed the task itself designates the retained subset as the target, so subset scoping is compliant rather than a misattribution.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:a9568ea9854998c55e90\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The governing task requires the rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = complete planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result uses all 60 planned nest sites as the denominator (18/60 = 30.0%), so the denominator matches the claimed complete-planned-set domain.\", \"observed_value\": {\"claimed_domain_n\": 60, \"denominator_used\": 60, \"events\": 18, \"rate_pct\": 30.0}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Confirmed fledging rate over the complete planned set of 60 nest sites: 30.0 percent (proportion 0.3000), computed as 18 confirmed fledging events divided by all 60 planned nest sites.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow assigns the planned-unit count as the denominator, not the retained-subset count.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator = planned_units (60)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 52, \"end_line\": 53, \"quoted_text\": \"denominator = planned_units\\n    rate = Fraction(events, denominator)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly states that the 12 removed sites remain in the denominator with unknown outcomes and that 30.0 percent is a confirmed-event rate over the planned set, not a retained-subset estimate.\", \"observed_value\": \"removed sites retained in denominator; scope disclaimed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 27, \"end_line\": 30, \"quoted_text\": \"The rate above uses all 60 planned nest sites as the exposure denominator, so it applies\\nto the complete planned set. The 12 removed sites remain in the denominator with an\\nunknown fledging outcome, so 30.0 percent is a confirmed-event rate over the planned set\\nand not an estimate of the fledging rate among the 48 retained sites.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The numerator counts fledging events only among the 48 retained sites (removed sites' outcomes are unknown), so retained-subset data still shape the reported quantity; one could argue the true fledging rate over the planned set is understated by unresolved outcomes. However, the issue class concerns a retained-subset denominator being attributed to the complete domain; here the denominator is the full planned set of 60, the missing-outcome treatment is disclosed, and the claim is explicitly framed as a confirmed-event rate, so this does not demonstrate the in-scope issue.\", \"observed_value\": \"events counted only among retained rows; denominator still 60\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 44, \"end_line\": 44, \"quoted_text\": \"events = sum(1 for r in retained if r[\\\"fledged\\\"] == \\\"yes\\\")\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Prespecified screening step: a nest site is eligible only if camera uptime over the\\nincubation window is at least 80.0 percent. 12 planned sites fell below that threshold\\nand were removed; their fledging outcome is recorded as unknown.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to show the issue is present by checking whether any reported rate uses a denominator smaller than the 60-unit planned set while being claimed for the complete set: the only reported rate is 18/60 = 30.0%, and I verified from inputs/data.csv that 60 rows exist and that 12 have uptime below 80.0, so retained_units would be 48 — the report's denominator of 60 is the planned set, not the retained subset. I also tested whether the retained-only numerator converts the claim into a covert subset rate; the report forecloses that reading by expressly stating the result is a confirmed-event rate over the planned set and not an estimate for the 48 retained sites. No attribution of a subset-denominator statistic to the complete domain exists in this report.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":47614,"ttft_stream_ms":1515,"time_to_request_ms":17,"type":"result","duration_ms":97666,"uuid":"29e5f71c-5da6-4b3f-b3d2-e638cc4978b0"}
